# .cursorrules

## Project Overview

**Brand:** Горький Клининг (Gorky Cleaning)  
**Domain:** gorkycleaning.ru  
**Geo:** Нижний Новгород

This project is a commercial cleaning company website built with:

* Next.js 15+
* React 19
* TypeScript
* Tailwind CSS 4
* shadcn/ui
* Radix UI
* Motion
* React Hook Form
* Zod
* Resend
* Telegram Bot API

The project must prioritize:

1. Conversion
2. SEO
3. Performance
4. Scalability
5. Maintainability

---

# Roadmap Progress Rules

**Source of truth:** `roadmap.md`

After every completed action, task, or subtask that maps to the roadmap:

* Update `roadmap.md` in the same session — do not defer.
* Mark completed items with `- [x]` (checkbox with x / крестик).
* Leave pending items as `- [ ]`.
* If a task is partially done, leave it unchecked and add a short note if needed.
* When an entire stage is complete, update the **Текущий этап** line at the top of `roadmap.md`.
* Never finish a roadmap-related task without updating progress in `roadmap.md`.

---

# General Rules

Always:

* Use TypeScript.
* Use strict typing.
* Prefer Server Components.
* Minimize Client Components.
* Write clean production-ready code.
* Follow Next.js App Router best practices.
* Avoid quick hacks.
* Avoid duplicated code.
* Prefer reusable abstractions.

Never:

* Use any.
* Use inline styles.
* Create giant components.
* Hardcode repeated values.
* Ignore accessibility.

---

# Architecture Rules

Follow this structure:

src/

app/

components/

features/

shared/

lib/

hooks/

constants/

types/

styles/

---

# Component Rules

Maximum component size:

300 lines

If larger:

Split into smaller components.

---

Use:

* feature components
* shared components
* ui components

Example:

features/home/hero

features/home/services

features/home/calculator

features/home/faq

---

# Naming Rules

Components:

PascalCase

Example:

HeroSection.tsx

ServicesCatalog.tsx

CalculatorForm.tsx

---

Hooks:

useSomething.ts

Example:

useLeadForm.ts

useMediaQuery.ts

---

Utilities:

camelCase

Example:

formatPrice.ts

sendTelegramLead.ts

---

# Styling Rules

Use:

Tailwind CSS

shadcn/ui

CSS variables

Design tokens

Never:

* write large custom CSS files
* use CSS frameworks besides Tailwind
* use inline style objects

---

# Design System Rules

Use design tokens only.

Spacing:

4
8
12
16
24
32
48
64
96
128

Radius:

12
20
28
36

Never invent random spacing values.

---

# Typography Rules

Font:

Inter

Fallback:

system-ui

Use semantic hierarchy.

Only:

H1

H2

H3

H4

Body

Small

Caption

---

# Accessibility Rules

Always:

* semantic HTML
* proper labels
* aria attributes
* keyboard navigation
* visible focus states

Target Lighthouse Accessibility:

95+

---

# Performance Rules

Target Lighthouse:

Performance 95+

SEO 100

Accessibility 95+

Best Practices 100

---

Always:

* optimize images
* use next/image
* lazy load heavy components
* use dynamic imports when needed

Never:

* import huge libraries unnecessarily
* block rendering

---

# SEO Rules

**Canonical domain:** https://gorkycleaning.ru

Every page must include:

* title
* description
* canonical
* open graph
* twitter card

Use Metadata API.

Generate structured data when relevant.

---

Supported schemas:

* LocalBusiness
* Service
* FAQ
* Review
* Breadcrumb

---

# Forms Rules

Use:

* React Hook Form
* Zod

Validation must exist for every field.

Never submit unvalidated data.

---

# Lead Handling Rules

All forms must support:

1. Telegram delivery
2. Email delivery via Resend

Lead payload:

* source
* page
* name
* phone
* service
* area

Always log failures.

---

# Animation Rules

Use Motion.

Animations must be:

* subtle
* fast
* premium

Avoid:

* excessive parallax
* bouncing effects
* distracting motion

Duration:

200ms–500ms

---

# Home Page Rules

Homepage sections:

1 Hero

2 Trust Metrics

3 Process

4 What's Included

5 Services Catalog

6 Cost Calculator

7 Statistics

8 Cases

9 Founder

10 Trust Dashboard

11 Work Process

12 Team

13 FAQ

14 CTA

15 Footer

Do not change section order without explicit request.

---

# Services Pages Rules

All service pages must use a shared template.

Structure:

Hero

Description

Benefits

Included Services

Pricing

Calculator

Cases

Reviews

FAQ

CTA

---

# Mobile Rules

Mobile-first development.

Support:

320px

360px

390px

430px

768px

1024px

1440px

1920px

No horizontal scrolling.

No layout shifts.

---

# Code Quality Rules

Before completing any task:

* remove dead code
* remove unused imports
* remove console logs
* remove duplicate logic

Always prefer:

* composition
* reusable components
* typed utilities

---

# Deployment Rules

Environment variables must never be hardcoded.

Use:

.env.local

.env.production

Validate env variables.

---

# Documentation Rules

For every major feature:

Create:

* purpose
* architecture
* dependencies
* usage notes

---

# Final Principle

Every implementation must satisfy:

1. Production-ready
2. SEO-friendly
3. Mobile-first
4. Accessible
5. Scalable
6. High-conversion
7. Clean architecture
8. Modern design system
9. Fast performance
10. Enterprise-level code quality
